<!--
  RESEARCH CONSENT GATE

  The research deployment's route "/" lands here, not on the module. Two
  states: unanswered, the consent form; answered either way, the module.
  The gate tests ANSWERED, never the value: declining changes nothing about
  what the student does.

  There is no in-platform place to change the answer afterwards. This is a
  one-hour activity; a student who changes their mind tells the instructor,
  and the response is excluded downstream.

  The module itself stays launchable, so the same content serves outside a
  study with no wrapper at all. Which consent-form version a student saw is
  recoverable from the release the event log ties back to.
-->

<Vertical id="temperance_study" title="READ 1000 — Temperance (Research Study)" launchable="true">
<Use ref="temperance_irb_consent_form" when="!@temperance_irb_consent.value" />
<Use ref="temperance_module"       when="@temperance_irb_consent.value" />

<!-- The form is defined here unrendered and shown through the <Use> above,
     so its state has one home. The text follows the consent form approved
     for the same protocol at the University of Memphis, with this course's
     materials and instructor. -->
<Hidden id="temperance_consent_defs">
<Vertical id="temperance_irb_consent_form" title="Research Consent">
<Markdown id="temperance_irb_consent_text">
## Informed Consent

**Title:** Scenario-Based Assessment in the age of generative AI: Making space in the education market for alternative assessment paradigms

**Principal Investigator:** Dr. John Sabatini

**Sponsor:** Institute for Intelligent Systems (IIS)

You are being asked to take part in a research study. If you decide to
take part, you will agree to share some of your course work with the
researchers: your responses in this reading module, including your answers,
highlights, and writing. These materials will be obtained after grades are
submitted and will be accessed only by the researchers.

No work beyond that which you would normally do as part of this course
will be required. The research will require no more time than you would
normally spend on the course. The decision to participate, or not to take
part, will have no effect on your grade or standing in this class. Your
instructor will not know whether you consented until after they submit the
grades for the course.

You do not have to be in this study, and you may choose to leave the study
at any time by telling your instructor; your responses will then be left
out of the research.

Questions: Professor Timothy Nelson, timothy.nelson@mtsu.edu.

Please choose one. Either answer takes you into the module.
</Markdown>
<ChoiceInput id="temperance_irb_consent">
  <Key id="temperance_irb_consent_consented" value="consented"> I agree to take part in the study.       </Key>
  <Key id="temperance_irb_consent_declined"  value="declined" > I do not want to take part in the study. </Key>
</ChoiceInput>
</Vertical> <!-- temperance_irb_consent_form -->
</Hidden>
</Vertical> <!-- temperance_study -->
